  "safety": {
   "cautions": [
    "Stop if you feel sharp, radiating or nerve-type pain.",
    "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG.",
    "Straight-leg raises load the low back (McGill 1998). If the back arches, hover higher or bend the knees.",
    "Neck discomfort: rest the head on the mat between legs or support it with one hand.",
    "Pregnancy and postpartum (diastasis recti): get individual guidance before trunk-flexion or straight-leg work."
   ],
